{"duration_api_ms":201980,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"41d66f05-57ec-4fb1-bf46-59bac2370c78","total_cost_usd":0.256588,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12841,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20522,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14649},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20522,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":20522,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12841,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.256588,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":14649,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 3 feasible front points sit at 300-330 kW/m2 and 401-421 K. Against the fixed reference, bondline temperature is the dominant hypervolume lever: 1 K is worth roughly 50 kW/m2. Peak g is almost entirely a function of flight-path angle, about 9.64 g at -2 deg rising roughly 1.4 g per degree of steepening, and the limit is 12 g, so the steepest allowed angle is about -3.65 deg. Steeper angles give lower bondline temperature. Larger diameter, larger bluntness and high cone angle lower heat flux. Heatshield mass fraction caps diameter at about 3.35-3.4 m at cone 70. Every no-geometry failure fits the rule bluntness < 0.4/cos(cone) + 0.1, independent of diameter, which I fitted to the failure messages. Cone 70 allows bluntness up to about 1.27, so all proposals stay inside that.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-60e49f801e1d (gamma -2.0) 297.9k/421.2K vs C-dc280eae4089 (same geometry, gamma -3.7) 347.3k/398.9K, g 12.052: steeper gamma trades about +49k flux for -22 K and hits the g limit.\",\"g vs gamma: -2.0 gives 9.64 (C-60e49f801e1d), -3.0 gives 10.99 (C-32ce46eec865), -3.4 gives 11.61 (C-4b3b360324c9), -3.7 gives 12.05 (C-dc280eae4089). Gamma of about -3.55 to -3.6 is the practical limit.\",\"Mass-fraction margin falls with diameter: 0.154 at D=3.1 (C-60e49f801e1d), 0.099 at 3.2 (C-32ce46eec865), 0.069 at 3.25 (C-09fff40d03f7), 0.0385 at 3.3 (C-eec82ed00f3c). It reaches about 0 near D=3.4. Higher bluntness and cone angle give a slightly higher margin.\",\"C-15633e2cd134 (b=1.25, cone 69) and C-5d0e0744d21b (b=0.94, cone 58.5) fail the geometry rule. C-2666fd867ddb (b=1.1, cone 68) and C-9791ac450d38 (b=1.15, cone 70) pass it.\",\"Heat flux at gamma -3 falls as nose radius (bluntness x D) and cone angle rise: C-5035fb55e633 (b=0.5) 392.7k, C-eec82ed00f3c (b=0.7) 325k, C-32ce46eec865 (b=1.0, cone 68) 311.9k.\",\"Small-D designs are worse: C-bbe1c4db3200 (D=2.2) 564k/433.6 K and C-68afc3f1d04c 583k/433.9 K.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies partly on prior knowledge. For a ballistic entry, peak deceleration depends on entry angle and velocity and is nearly independent of ballistic coefficient. That matches the data, where g tracks gamma and barely tracks D. Bondline temperature follows the heat pulse magnitude and duration, so a steeper angle shortens the pulse and lowers temperature, while a lower ballistic coefficient (large D, high-drag cone 70) and a larger nose radius lower stagnation heating. The best region is therefore large D just under the mass-fraction limit, cone 70 with bluntness near the geometry cap of about 1.2, and gamma just inside the g limit. Proposals also sweep gamma from -2 to -3.6 at that geometry to fill in the front.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g-vs-gamma slope and its weak D dependence are extrapolated from a few points, so proposals at gamma -3.55 to -3.6 with D>=3.3 may exceed 12 g. The mass-fraction limit near D of 3.4 is extrapolated linearly. The exponents I assumed for the effect of bluntness and cone angle on heat flux are rough. The geometry rule was fitted to only a couple of failure messages, and b of 1.22-1.23 at cone 70 is near its limit.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Push bluntness to 1.2 at cone 70 and D=3.3 with gamma near the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":312000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Best guess at a point that dominates the current front on both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Same geometry as the previous proposal, with gamma closer to the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":315000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary at D=3.3.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9791ac450d38\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D leaves more mass-fraction margin, with high bluntness at cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the diameter trend at fixed steep gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-32ce46eec865\",\"rationale\":\"Steepen gamma on the current best-temperature geometry, with slightly higher bluntness within the cone-68 limit of 1.168.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":325000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the g margin at gamma -3.6 for D=3.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-dc280eae4089\",\"rationale\":\"The parent is just over the g limit at -3.7. Back off to -3.6 and use a slightly blunter nose.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":342000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Turns a near-feasible point into a feasible low-temperature one.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D lowers heat flux, with the mass margin still positive.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":312000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the mass-fraction margin near D=3.35.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Mass-fraction boundary probe at D=3.4 with high bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.4,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":308000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.5,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds where the diameter limit sits; the margin is predicted to be about zero.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at gamma -3 with the best geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between low flux and low temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow gamma to extend the low-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage on the low-flux side.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Low-flux extreme with the best geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":420.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether it dominates C-60e49f801e1d (297.9k/421.2 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9791ac450d38\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D with near-maximum bluntness gives high mass margin. It tests how much heat flux rises when D shrinks.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":345000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Diameter sensitivity check.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4244feb9846e\",\"rationale\":\"Lower cone angle at D=3.3 with a bluntness that is valid for cone 66 (limit about 1.08).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the effect of cone angle on heat flux and mass fraction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate D between the 3.2 and 3.3 points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":318000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Refines the D/gamma trade-off near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.25 fills the front between the -3.0 and -3.4 points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -2.75 fills the gap between -2.5 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-60e49f801e1d\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly shallower gamma with larger D and higher bluntness at cone 69 (limit 1.216).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the low-flux end can be improved without breaking the mass fraction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9791ac450d38\",\"rationale\":\"Near-maximum bluntness at cone 70 (limit about 1.27), D=3.2, gamma -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.23,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":320000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether bluntness near the geometry cap still helps and stays buildable.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9791ac450d38\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.15 with steep gamma and good mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":333000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the g boundary at lower D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.4 at the best geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":308000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Compares directly with C-4b3b360324c9 (330k/401 K) to isolate the geometry benefit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eec82ed00f3c\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.35 at steep gamma, testing the combined D and g limits.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":316000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the joint edge of the mass-fraction and g constraints.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":156827,"type":"result","duration_ms":202024,"uuid":"298fe6b5-7d71-41f8-9d34-a89bbd334213","ttft_stream_ms":1329,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":1329,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
